ory", "education", "Turkey", "museum"], "long_description": "October 1927, Ankara. Take a seat in the parliament hall as afternoon light streams through the tall windows. The rostrum is empty; above it, the lines of Nutuk, Atat\u00fcrk's great speech, appear one by one, each with its meaning in today's Turkish.\n\n- 18 chapters, from the landing at Samsun to the Address to the Youth.\n- The Road to Independence: a relief map of Anatolia on a tactics board with 12 stops, from Istanbul to Izmir. Point at a pin to open that chapter on the rostrum.\n- Timeline and \"Did you know?\" boards on the walls of the hall.\n- Read at your own pace or let the lines advance on their own.\n- Touch controllers or hand tracking. Teleport by pointing at the floor; snap turn with the thumbstick. Comfortable seated or standing.\n- Works offline. No ads, no accounts, no data collection.\n\nThe app's text is in Turkish. Atat\u00fcrk's works are in the public domain; the original lines were checked against the full text of Nutuk on Wikisource.", "short_description": "Sit in the 1927 Turkish Parliament hall: the original lines of Atat\u00fcrk's Nutuk appear above the empty rostrum with their meaning in today's Turkish beneath, while a relief map of the road to independence waits on the table in front of you."}]}, "developer_name": "Mr. Anduv!", "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://emreanduv.github.io/nutuk-salonu/gizlilik.html?v=2", "developer_terms_of_service_url": null, "publisher_name": "Mr. Anduv!", "support_website_url": "https://github.com/emreanduv/nutuk-akisi/issues", "website_url": "https://emreanduv.github.io/nutuk-salonu/", "category": null, "comfort_rating": "COMFORTABLE_FOR_MOST", "comfort_tags": [], "context_category": {"id": "362692211442873", "context_category": "APPS"}, "context_topics": [{"id": "1043107547362485"}, {"id": "726368587961803"}], "external_subscription_type": "NOT_REQUIRED", "genres": [], "has_in_app_ads": null, "internet_connection": "REQUIRED", "play_are